        "original_id": "580d56d4-2bd5-51b7-9b36-b09b9dfd3f03",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Royal Albert Hall, London, South Kensington, Wolverhampton Civic Hall, Paradiso, Amsterdam, La Luna, Brussels\n- Products: Live Wood, The Best of Nanci Griffith\n- Events: concerts, Proms concerts\n\nFacts:\n- Since 1941, the Royal Albert Hall in South Kensington, London, has hosted the Proms concerts annually each summer.\n- In June 1993, the previously unreleased song \"The Road To Aberdeen\" on The Best of Nanci Griffith was recorded live at the Royal Albert Hall in London.\n- On 22 November 1993, songs for Live Wood were chosen from a concert at the Royal Albert Hall in London, although the date was incorrectly listed as December.\n- On 9 March 1994, songs for Live Wood were chosen from a concert at Wolverhampton Civic Hall.\n- On 16 April 1994, songs for Live Wood were chosen from a concert at Paradiso in Amsterdam.\n- On 17 April 1994, songs for Live Wood were chosen from a concert at La Luna in Brussels.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "e35a66d4-2cc3-5600-83b1-d38f89508d80",
        "text": "Page: Live Wood. Sentence: Songs were chosen from a number of the concerts, including the Royal Albert Hall, London (22 November 1993 - incorrectly listed as December), Wolverhampton Civic Hall (9 March 1994), the Paradiso in Amsterdam (16 April 1994) and La Luna, Brussels (17 April 1994).\nPage: Royal Albert Hall. Sentence: The Royal Albert Hall is a concert hall on the northern edge of South Kensington, London, which holds the Proms concerts annually each summer since 1941.\nPage: The Best of Nanci Griffith. Sentence: The second previously unreleased song \"The Road To Aberdeen\" was recorded live at The Royal Albert Hall, London in June 1993.",
